      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-terminal-branching-casimir",
      "title": "The Casimir scalar of a compact type at the end of the lowering",
      "hypotheses": "τ is a unitary representation of H=U(r,s) with its smooth derived action. V is a nonzero finite-dimensional compact irreducible of highest weight L=μ+ρn−ρc for strictly decreasing μ. Its first noncompact derivative layer contains no nonzero compact highest vector of weight L−(ea−eb) with a<b and opposite signs.",
